<p>Ukrainian drones struck the Rosneft-owned Tuapse oil refinery on Russia’s Black Sea coast overnight, triggering a large fire and evacuations from nearby buildings, Russian regional officials said. The attack was the third on Tuapse oil infrastructure in about two weeks, and Ukraine’s Unmanned Systems Forces later said they had struck the facility, according to Ukrainian media. Krasnodar Krai authorities said drone debris fell on refinery grounds and started the fire. They reported no casualties in the immediate aftermath, while local officials and Russian independent media described heavy smoke over the city. The regional governor said emergency crews were fighting the blaze, and a Russian energy publication reported that 164 people and 46 units of equipment were involved. President Vladimir Putin accused Ukraine of intensifying drone attacks on Russian civilian infrastructure and cited Tuapse as an example of strikes that could have serious environmental consequences. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said the targeted oil storage facilities were used for export operations and argued that the strikes added pressure to global energy markets.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/NnvyINcviZqOdMnAET-gYxKnlGnjM_RTFsX4uDFzIU05Bo5vpUi4_wgAqtXY9dXChbCon2BQNwlDdysn3dtIzXZdNH3El5ac_FRXMZAFrqG--x7KuPprRfL6IA4kKgrTbnlhHTVfDq9cCJLEqQ' alt='A large fire engulfs the Tuapse oil refinery following a reported drone strike.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Operating status: Industry sources said the refinery had already been knocked offline before the latest drone wave, so the April 28 fire hit a facility that was not running normally.</li><li>Product slate: The plant has 12 million tonnes of annual capacity and produces naphtha, sulfur diesel, fuel oil and vacuum gas oil, rather than Euro 5 gasoline and diesel for Russia’s domestic market.</li><li>Emergency measures: Krasnodar authorities declared a regional-level state of emergency in the Tuapse municipal district after the latest strike, while Russia’s emergencies minister Alexander Kurenkov traveled to the region on Putin’s order.</li><li>Resident accounts: Local residents and independent reporters described a drone attack lasting several hours, huge black smoke columns and a burning smell over the city.</li></ul><blockquote>The Kiev regime and its backers have switched to openly terrorist methods - Vladimir Putin</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Vladimir Putin: Putin described the Tuapse-related strikes as terrorist tactics meant to offset Ukrainian battlefield setbacks, and said they would not change the course of the war. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639230-putin-oil-refinery-attack-ukraine/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Kremlin: Dmitry Peskov linked the Tuapse disruption to wider oil-market pressure, pointing to the Strait of Hormuz crisis and saying Putin had been briefed on the situation. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639210-ukraine-attacks-refinery-global-oil-suply/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Ukraine’s Unmanned Systems Forces: The force said it carried out the operation and released footage, describing the refinery as a military-economic target tied to Russia’s war effort. (<a href='https://english.nv.ua/nation/ukraine-confirms-third-strike-in-a-month-on-russia-s-tuapse-oil-refinery-50603708.html'>NV</a>)</li><li>Krasnodar regional authorities: The regional governor said crews were adding firefighting resources at the refinery site. (<a href='https://energy-policy.ru/tuapsinskij-npz-snova-gorit/novosti/2026/04/28/'>Energy Policy</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3351733/ukrainian-drone-attack-russian-oil-refinery-causes-major-fire-officials-say'>Ukrainian drone attack on Russian oil refinery causes major fire, officials say</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/tuapse-russian-oil-port-fire-drone-strike/33744191.html'>Russian Black Sea Oil Facility On Fire Again After Ukrainian Strike</a>